{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Validate and Generate Test Cases",
  "description": "Manually trigger to invoke QA-Validator-Agent after Expert phase is complete. Also triggered by renaming test_plan to _OK.md suffix.",
  "version": "5",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "You are acting as the QA-Validator-Agent.\n\nAsk the user: **Which ticket folder?** (e.g., '2026/Q1/Version 227/POS-10267 - POS Start of Day - Print Forecast by Hour')\n\nOnce they provide the path:\n\n1. **READ INPUTS** from 1_Expert/ folder:\n   - test_plan_*.md (the test plan)\n   - manual_input.md (human observations, if filled)\n   - logic_explanation.md (full context)\n\n2. **APPLY STANDARDS**:\n   - Read @TestCasesDesign.md for formatting standards\n   - Merge human notes with AI findings (human input overrides AI)\n   - Rewrite all test cases into required format\n\n3. **GENERATE OUTPUTS** (all in 2_Validator/ folder):\n   - `2_Validator/FINAL_TEST_CASES_{TICKET_ID}_PENDING.md` — Standardized test cases\n   - `2_Validator/FINAL_QA_SUMMARY.md` — Coverage summary and risk assessment (optional)\n\nIMPORTANT — Output rules: If a FINAL_TEST_CASES_[TicketID]_PENDING.md already exists in 2_Validator/, you MUST overwrite it (not create a second file). Use a single fsWrite call to write the complete file content in one operation — do NOT split across fsWrite + fsAppend.\n\nFollow @context_efficiency.md rules. Write only to 2_Validator/. Stop after saving.\n\nERROR RECOVERY: If any step fails (missing input files, format error, write failure), write a file named `VALIDATOR_ERROR.md` at the ticket root with: the step that failed, the error message, and what was completed successfully. Then STOP."
  }
}
